-- title:
--   Every prime of the integral Hecke algebra comes from a normalised eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. Let $\mathfrak p \subseteq \mathbb{T}$ be a prime ideal. Then there exists a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of the predicate [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L28), i.e. its $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff f n` at the cusp $\infty$ (with period $1$) satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m, n$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\, a_{p^{r}}$ for every prime $p \nmid N$ and every $r$, and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for every prime $p \mid N$ and every $r$; and such that every $t \in \mathbb{T}$ with $t f = 0$ as an endomorphism applied to $f$ lies in $\mathfrak p$. Thus the $\mathbb{T}$-annihilator of $f$ is contained in $\mathfrak p$; equality of the annihilator with $\mathfrak p$ is not asserted.
--
--   This is the passage from a prime ideal of the integral Hecke algebra to an actual normalised eigenform realising it — the Deligne–Serre style eigenform realisation step with which level-lowering arguments conclude. It is used in the treatment of the Hecke operator $U_q$ at primes of bad reduction and in the production of newforms attached to points of the relevant Hecke-algebra spectrum.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_annihilator_le_of_isPrime.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_annihilator_le_of_isPrime {N : ℕ} [NeZero N]
    (S : Set ℕ) (𝔭 : Ideal (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S)) (h𝔭 : 𝔭.IsPrime) :
    ∃ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2, f.IsNormalizedEigenform ∧
      ∀ t : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S,
        (t : Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2)) f = 0 → t ∈ 𝔭 := by sorry
